## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/weave.html
- Summary (EN): Generates a woven fabric texture by interlacing horizontal weft fibres and vertical warp fibres. Useful for fabric, basket-weave and similar textile patterns.
- Résumé (FR) : Génère une texture de tissage en entrelaçant des fibres de trame et de chaîne, avec réglage des rangées, colonnes, croisements et ombrages.

- Inputs meaning: ["size_ref: reference layer that sets the output image size and metadata", "pattern (optional): Mono layer supplying a custom over/under arrangement"]

- Key parameters: ["Rows / Columns: number of weft (horizontal) and warp (vertical) fibres", "Weave Multiplier: increases the number of over/under crossings for a tighter weave", "Arrangement (Every Nth Column, Every Nth Tile, Checkerboard): controls which fibres pass over at each tile, including a classic plain-weave checkerboard", "Row Inset / Column Inset: gap spacing between rows and between columns", "Edge Gradient: softens fibre edges for a rounder profile", "Overlap Gradient / Overlap Gradient Ramp: shading at crossings and its falloff", "Fiber Scale / Fiber Strength: fineness, elongation and intensity of procedural strand detail"]

- Caveats: ["The Arrangement parameters are disabled when a custom arrangement is connected to the pattern input, which overrides them"]

